#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:46
#: 15bab6f410af47a2a750a5d74f75fc7b
msgid "On a Windows machine a \"PX4Flow\" device should appear in Connection drop-down of the Mission Planner (and the Windows Device Manager), or be automatically recognized by QGroundControl.  If it does not you may need to download, unzip and manually install the `px4flow windows driver <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/px4flow_win_driver.zip>`__ which may in turn require allowing installing unsigned drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:49
#: b3bd371cdba94483803efa8757444194
msgid "Using MissionPlanner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:51
#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:78
#: 217eb182a485412eb73da0647887b06b
#: a4f8f5bc3cc14a398af33c953a73fed6
msgid "Download and unzip the `PX4Flow-KLT firmware <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/px4flow-klt-06Dec2014.zip>`__ (`source code here <https://github.com/priseborough/px4flow/tree/klt_flow>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:54
#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:74
#: 14cc2eece3854930a4f191a615f2668d
#: c2e2994c584344c9873b4580312ee10e
msgid "Connect the PX4Flow sensor to your computer using a micro USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:55
#: 56a48cc2ec7f4b96854829799f08f3a7
msgid "Open the Initial Setup, Install Firmware screen, select the COM port and click the \"Load custom firmware\" link.  Select the px4flow-klt-06dec2014.px4 binary you downloaded in Step 1.  You may need to unplug and plug back in the sensor to start the upload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:60
#: b27d7ddae57c4ecca1b1d298e6f7dbfb
msgid "Disconnect and reconnect the sensor/USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:61
#: 85d30ac390d34a6c8e282c3d2f3053cb
msgid "Select the appropriate COM port and press Connect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:62
#: 24643753f80847439a15138093955197
msgid "Open the Initial Setup > Optional Hardware > PX4Flow screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:63
#: a6d5f841f02b473a9dd841c46f2200eb
msgid "Remove the lens cap and point the camera at a high contrast object at least 3m away.  Remove the small screw that stops the lens from turning and adjust the focus until the image appears clearly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:70
#: 3969498cdf3342dbbaa6955f3877efb2
msgid "Using QGroundControl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:71
#: 45d0e1fd83f5438a9d20423792e9cd3e
msgid "In order to use QgroundControl, PX4Flow and ArduPilot, you will need to complete setup and focussing with the firmware loaded by QGroundControl, and then update the firmware to be compatible with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:73
#: 262b36fca57845d9b990e90f3fece2d6
msgid "Select the Vehicle Setup page, and click the Firmware tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:75
#: 91848cbfd1f94d229d083da00674531c
msgid "Check the \"Standard Version (stable)\" is selected in the right hand pane. Click \"OK\". QGroundControl will flash a firmware that can be used to focus the lens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:76
#: 83f1357ff53f4ceab05143a24370237a
msgid "Unplug and replug the sensor. Two extra tabs should appear: \"PX4Flow\" and \"Parameters\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:77
#: c5342e9fb0074671a707606f576fdbcd
msgid "Click \"PX4Flow\", remove the lens cap and point the camera at a high contrast object at least 3m away.  Remove the small screw that stops the lens from turning and adjust the focus until the image appears clearly.  This will focus the device to infinity.  Refit the screw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:80
#: 2d6fc9921e0b493092f77a7bb1ac4820
msgid "Unplug the sensor, click on the \"Firmware\" tab and replug the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:81
#: aa6816abf4c64477a9b5196a1997be50
msgid "On the right hand side, click on the firmware version dropdown, and select \"Custom firmware file\".  Click \"OK\".  Then select the firmware downloaded above.  QGroundControl should now flash a firmware compatible with ArduPilot.  QGroundControl will now think that the sensor is a Pixhawk.  Dont worry.  Unplug it, and connect it to your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:84
#: 22e1cddc93c9407180e92454a198bbe7
msgid "Connect to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:89
#: 89866cb222b24e37af57313b21e8f433
msgid "The sensor should be connected to the autopilot via the 4-pin I2C port.  In most cases an I2C splitter should be used to allow other I2C devices (like the external RGB LED and GPS/Compass module's compass) to share the same port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:94
#: 748197b3dd2e4210be7431a5f436a074
msgid "Mounting to the Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:96
#: a46207faa51d4b17bce0d478a409a78c
msgid "The default mounting of the flow sensor is for it to be pointing straight down with the micro USB port pointing towards the front of the vehicle. On the back of the sensor you should see the axis printed, the X axis should point forwards and the Y axis to the right. The :ref:`FLOW_ORIENT_YAW <copter:FLOW_ORIENT_YAW>` parameter can be used to account for other yaw orientations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:100
#: 93e5ff4fc37747f8b5a4458de34fd052
msgid "It is important that the flow sensor be mounted where it does not experience angular vibration that could blur the image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:105
#: fdbbd71bcd674a7eb1082070b0d554e8
msgid "The default mounting orientation is different to that shown on the \\ `PX4FLOW wiki <https://docs.px4.io/master/en/sensor/px4flow.html>`__. If you mount the board as shown in the \\ `PX4FLOW wiki <https://docs.px4.io/master/en/sensor/px4flow.html>`__, you will need to set :ref:`FLOW_ORIENT_YAW <copter:FLOW_ORIENT_YAW>` to -9000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:111
#: 1c9fb9e4383f4b93851fd40174409dcf
msgid "Enabling the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:116
#: b317f61a906246739506b2cd4b42924d
msgid "The sensor can be enabled by connecting to the autopilot with the Mission Planner and then on the **Initial Setup \\| Optional Hardware \\| Optical Flow** page check the **Enable** checkbox.  Alternatively the :ref:`FLOW_TYPE <copter:FLOW_TYPE>` parameter should be set to \"1\" through the full parameters list.  The sensor will be initialised once the Pixhawk board is rebooted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4flow-overview.rst:122
#: 1c19dec230cb4c25abd256dbc7f79a43
msgid "If the sensor is reported to be unhealthy, it may help to set :ref:`BRD_BOOT_DELAY <BRD_BOOT_DELAY>` to 600 (0.6 seconds) and reboot the autopilot.  This will give more time for the sensor to start-up before the autopilot probes for it on the I2C bus."
msgstr ""

